The tick hands the processor on without putting the preempted thread back on its share's ring.
The thread would stay ready and never run again;
every ready thread with a share but the running one is on its share's ring.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a waiting or ready thread is on no queue

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -431,7 +431,6 @@ void sched_tick(uint32_t ticks)
     if (was != NULL) {
         share_settle(was);
     }
-    enqueue(current);
     turn = next_turn();
     run_turn();
 }
